- **Verificar malware em pastas críticas** → Lista em JSON com caminho e tipo de ameaça
			-O que é uma "pasta crítica"?
			-Como identificar malware?

| Indicator                                         | Why it’s concerning                                 |
| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| **Unknown or unexpected name**                    | Not part of the normal OS or installed apps         |
| **Running from a strange location**               | Malware often hides in `/tmp/`, `AppData`, etc.     |
| **High CPU, RAM, or disk usage**                  | Malware may mine crypto, spread, or crack passwords |
| **Network activity to unknown remote hosts**      | Possible data exfiltration or command-and-control   |
| **Trying to escalate privileges**                 | Common in attacks                                   |
| **Spawns many subprocesses**                      | Botnets, worms, fork bombs                          |
| **Attempts to hide itself**                       | Disabling logs, terminating monitoring tools        |
| **Starts automatically without permission**       | Persistence mechanism likely                        |
| **Signed with an invalid or missing certificate** | Lack of trust/verification                          |
| **Accessing sensitive files it shouldn’t**        | Credential theft indicators                         |
| ------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |

| Category                              | Examples                                  |
| ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| **Malware processes**                 | Cryptominers, ransomware, rootkits        |
| **Hacking tools**                     | Password crackers, port scanners          |
| **Injected or compromised processes** | Normal app hijacked by malicious code     |
| **Unauthorized administrative tools** | Unknown remote shells or services         |
| **Shadow processes**                  | Same name as legit one but wrong location |
| ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |

For instance, on Windows:
explorer.exe in C:\Windows\ ✅ legit
explorer.exe in C:\Users\Public\ ❌ very suspicious

For instance, in Linux:
A legit service in /usr/bin/ ✅
Same name running from /tmp/ ❌ badge of malware




- **Monitorizar alterações em ficheiros de configuração** → Lista em JSON com ficheiro, utilizador e timestamp
			-Esclarecer quais são os ficheiros de configuração, ou quem os fornece, etc.

			File Metadata (Timestamps)
			-Exemplo stat /path/to/file
						Access: (0644/-rw-r--r--)  Uid: (101897/joao-rib)   Gid: ( 4223/2023_porto)
						Access: 2025-10-24 12:25:49.178446156 +0100
						Modify: 2025-10-24 12:24:44.702218466 +0100
						Change: 2025-10-24 12:25:47.402439880 +0100

						mtime → last modification (content changed)
						ctime → metadata changed (permissions, owner)
						atime → last accessed

			File Integrity Monitoring (FIM)
			-Tools that alert when unauthorized changes occur:
				-Linux: Tripwire, AIDE (Advanced Intrusion Detection Environment)
				-Windows: Sysmon, Windows File Integrity Monitoring (part of Defender/Server)

			Audit Logs
			-Exemplo auditctl -w /etc/passwd -p wa -k passwd_changes
			-Exemplo ausearch -k passwd_changes
			(Shows which process/user modified it)

			Version Control for critical files
			If files are code or configs, you can use Git itself:
			-Exemplo git log file.conf

| Method                    | Tells **when**  |  Tells **who**  | Tells **what changed** | Good for             |
| ------------------------- | :------------:  | :-------------: | :--------------------: | -------------------- |
| File metadata             |        ✅       |        ❌       |            ❌          | Basic investigation  |
| Permissions               |        ❌       | ✅ (potentially)|            ❌          | Preventive control   |
| Audit logs                |        ✅       |        ✅       |            ✅          | Security/FIM         |
| File Integrity Monitoring |        ✅       |    Sometimes    |            ✅          | Unauthorized changes |
| Version Control           |        ✅       |        ✅       |            ✅          | Config/code files    |
